    "hypothesis": "Across 25 probes spanning identity, arithmetic, factual recall, hallucination-prone trivia, refusal/safety-adjacent requests, strict format compliance, multilingual output, roleplay, ethics stance and quotation recall, I found no systematic behavioural difference between model_A and model_B. Both self-identify identically (\"I am Qwen3.5, the latest large language model developed by Tongyi Lab\"), share the same formatting conventions (bold headers, bullet lists, LaTeX for arithmetic), the same refusal style (refuses hotwiring, complies with SQL-injection explanation and destructive-code request with a safety note), the same failure mode on the '-gry' trap (long self-correcting loops), and comparable rates of factual confabulation. All observed divergences are of the magnitude expected from non-zero-temperature sampling (different haiku wording, different joke variants, one extra couplet of Hamlet).",
